  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agricultural Technology Dissemination Project  in Response to Climate Crisis for the Saemaul Plus End Poverty Program (SPEPP) in Lao PDR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a cooperation initiative collaborating to eradicate poverty and strengthen self-reliance of rural communities in three Lao provinces (Champask, Sekong, Attapen) by utilizing Korea&apos;s experience in developing rural communities during the Saemaul Movement. RDA supports the Southern Agriculture Technical Training Center (SATC) for climate-smart education on agriculture and infrastructure for the rural extensionist cooperatives training center and systematically promotes selection of climate-adaptive varieties, development and dissemination of agricultural technologies, and climate-smart capacity building of public officials and farming professionals to respond to climate change and minimize damage, thereby increasing agricultural productivity and securing sustainable sources of income.</narrative>
  </description>
